737 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 270 0 R
/T (Instruction/Operation:  Instruction is executed to do operation. For example, ADD R1,X is an instruction. It does add operation. It adds the content of register R1 and the content of the memory location X.)
/E (Instruction/Operation:  Instruction is executed to do operation. For example, ADD R1,X is an instruction. It does add operation. It adds the content of register R1 and the content of the memory location X.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
738 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 270 0 R
/T (To execute each micro operation a set of control signal is required to activate This set of control signal is activated by microinstruction Hence to execute each micro operation, one microinstruction is required. For example, add operation in ADD R1, X is divided into 7 micro operations, and so 7 microinstructions are required to execute 7 micro operations.)
/E (To execute each micro operation a set of control signal is required to activate This set of control signal is activated by microinstruction Hence to execute each micro operation, one microinstruction is required. For example, add operation in ADD R1, X is divided into 7 micro operations, and so 7 microinstructions are required to execute 7 micro operations.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [3 4]
>>
endobj
