1072 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 280 0 R
/T (Certain rows and columns can be deleted from the cover table to simplify determination of the minimal MCC covers 1. Column Cj contains only one X, which occurs in row Ci, Ci is said to be an essential MCC and must appear in every minimal MCC cover, since it only covers Cj Example: Column a and column  c contain only one X. So C1 and C2 are two essential MCC and must appear in every minimal MCC cover since C1 is only MCC that covers the control signal a and C2 is only MCC that covers the control signal c 2. All rows corresponding  to essential MCCs can be deleted from the cover table and all columns with X in essential rows can be deleted Hence deletes row C1, C2 and columns a, c, d. 3. If the cover table contains two identical columns then all but one of these columns can be deleted. Example: there is no identical columns)
/E (Certain rows and columns can be deleted from the cover table to simplify determination of the minimal MCC covers 1. Column Cj contains only one X, which occurs in row Ci, Ci is said to be an essential MCC and must appear in every minimal MCC cover, since it only covers Cj Example: Column a and column  c contain only one X. So C1 and C2 are two essential MCC and must appear in every minimal MCC cover since C1 is only MCC that covers the control signal a and C2 is only MCC that covers the control signal c 2. All rows corresponding  to essential MCCs can be deleted from the cover table and all columns with X in essential rows can be deleted Hence deletes row C1, C2 and columns a, c, d. 3. If the cover table contains two identical columns then all but one of these columns can be deleted. Example: there is no identical columns)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [42 43]
>>
endobj
1073 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /Figure
/P 280 0 R
/Pg 24 0 R
/A [2139 0 R 0]
/K [44]
>>
endobj
1074 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 281 0 R
/T (4. Column Ci is said to dominate column Cj if Ci contains an X in every row where Cj contains an X and Ci contains more X than Cj The dominating column can be deleted as every MCC that covers Cj automatically covers Ci Example: d dominates b and c while g dominates f , hence deletes column g 5. Row Ci is said to dominate row Cj if Ci contains an X in every columns where Cj contains an X and Ci contains more X than Cj In this case the dominating row Cj can be deleted, since Ci covers all the control signals that are covered by Cj Example: There is no such dominating row.)
/E (4. Column Ci is said to dominate column Cj if Ci contains an X in every row where Cj contains an X and Ci contains more X than Cj The dominating column can be deleted as every MCC that covers Cj automatically covers Ci Example: d dominates b and c while g dominates f , hence deletes column g 5. Row Ci is said to dominate row Cj if Ci contains an X in every columns where Cj contains an X and Ci contains more X than Cj In this case the dominating row Cj can be deleted, since Ci covers all the control signals that are covered by Cj Example: There is no such dominating row.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [0 1]
>>
endobj
