1099 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 281 0 R
/T (Step-3: Inspect each minimal MCC cover {Ci} in turn and determine all ways of including each control signal in exactly one subset of some Ci The minimal cover for this table contains two MCCs, possible choices are {C3, C8} and {C4, C7} Combining these with essential MCCs C1 and C2 the desired MCC solutions are {C1, C2, C3, C8} and {C1, C2, C4, C7}. Consider one of the two minimal MCC, say {C1, C2, C3, C8}.  There is only one way to cover a \(by C1\), b \(by C3\), c \(by C2\), e \(by C3\), f,g,h \(by C8\). There is two way to cover d \(by C2 and C3\). )
/E (Step-3: Inspect each minimal MCC cover {Ci} in turn and determine all ways of including each control signal in exactly one subset of some Ci The minimal cover for this table contains two MCCs, possible choices are {C3, C8} and {C4, C7} Combining these with essential MCCs C1 and C2 the desired MCC solutions are {C1, C2, C3, C8} and {C1, C2, C4, C7}. Consider one of the two minimal MCC, say {C1, C2, C3, C8}.  There is only one way to cover a \(by C1\), b \(by C3\), c \(by C2\), e \(by C3\), f,g,h \(by C8\). There is two way to cover d \(by C2 and C3\). )
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [26 27]
>>
endobj
